# 🧩 12. Complete Simple Bank

```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.20;

contract SimpleBank {

    mapping(address => uint256) public balances;

    // Deposit ETH
    function deposit() external payable {

        balances[msg.sender] += msg.value;

    }

    // Get user's recorded deposit
    function getMyBalance()
        external
        view
        returns(uint256)
    {
        return balances[msg.sender];
    }

    // Get contract's actual ETH balance
    function getContractBalance()
        external
        view
        returns(uint256)
    {
        return address(this).balance;
    }

}
```

---

# 🔍 13. How This Contract Works

### Step 1

Alice calls:

```text
deposit()
```

and sends:

```text
1 ETH
```

---

### Step 2

Solidity gives us:

```text
msg.sender = Alice
msg.value  = 1 ETH
```

---

### Step 3

Contract executes:

```solidity
balances[msg.sender] += msg.value;
```

Equivalent to:

```solidity
balances[Alice] += 1 ether;
```

---

### Step 4

The contract now holds:

```text
1 ETH
```

Therefore:

```solidity
address(this).balance
```

returns:

```text
1 ETH
```

