# 💰 16. `msg.value` vs `address(this).balance`

| `msg.value`                  | `address(this).balance`              |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| ETH attached to current call | Total ETH currently held by contract |
| Applies to current message   | Contract's current balance           |
| Can be 0                     | Can be any available balance         |
| Example: 1 ETH sent now      | Example: contract holds 10 ETH       |

---

## Example

Suppose the contract already has:

```text
10 ETH
```

Alice sends:

```text
2 ETH
```

During the transaction:

```text
msg.value = 2 ETH
```

The contract's balance after receiving the ETH becomes:

```text
address(this).balance = 12 ETH
```

---

# 💡 Remember

> **`msg.value` = ETH coming in with THIS call**

> **`address(this).balance` = ETH currently inside THIS contract**

