# 📥 21. `payable` Function vs `receive()`

Both can receive Ether, but they are used differently.

---

## Payable Function

```solidity
function deposit() external payable {

}
```

User explicitly calls:

```text
deposit()
```

---

## Receive Function

```solidity
receive() external payable {

}
```

Triggered by a direct Ether transfer with empty calldata when `receive()` is available and payable.

---

## Comparison

| Feature           | Payable Function    | `receive()`         |
| ----------------- | ------------------- | ------------------- |
| Called explicitly | ✅                  | ❌                  |
| Can receive ETH   | ✅                  | ✅                  |
| Has function name | ✅                  | ❌                  |
| Has parameters    | Can have parameters | ❌                  |
| Example           | `deposit()`         | Direct ETH transfer |
| Purpose           | Specific operation  | Plain ETH reception |

