# 🎯 Golden Rules

- 💰 **`payable` = allows Ether to be received.**
- 👤 **`msg.sender` = WHO called the function.**
- 💵 **`msg.value` = HOW MUCH Ether was sent with the call.**
- 🏦 **`address(this).balance` = Ether currently held by the contract.**
- 👤 **`address(user).balance` = Ether currently held by that address.**
- 📊 **`balances[user]` = application-specific accounting stored in your contract.**
- 🏦 A contract has its own Ether balance.
- 📥 A deposit function is normally declared `payable`.
- 🧩 `balances[msg.sender] += msg.value` connects the caller with the amount they deposited.
- ⚠️ Native ETH balance and an application's internal accounting are not automatically the same thing.
- 🔐 Withdrawal functions must be designed carefully to avoid reentrancy and other security issues.

